---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import GatewayCard from '@/components/ia/GatewayCard.astro';
import { governanceDecisionRegisters } from '@/data/governance-decisions';
---
<Layout
  title="Governance"
  description="How OPDA is governed: constitutional authority, standards development, conformance, change management, lifecycle and risk."
>
      <h1>Governance</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        How OPDA is governed, who has authority, how standards are developed, and which
        rules are ratified, practised or still proposed. The wider context includes the
        Trust Over IP model, the Digital Markets, Competition and Consumers Act 2024 and
        coordination through the Digital Property Market Steering Group.
      </p>

      <h2 id="decisions">Decision records</h2>
      <p>
        Significant choices are recorded so their context, authority and consequences can
        be reviewed. <a href="/governance/decisions">See how the three decision registers fit together</a>.
      </p>
      <div class="card-grid">
        {governanceDecisionRegisters.map((register) => <GatewayCard {...register} />)}
      </div>

      <h2 id="uk-initiative-context">UK initiative context</h2>
      <p>The legislation, departments, and forums that frame OPDA's mandate.</p>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <a class="card" href="/governance/uk-initiative">
          <div class="pill pill--brand">Start here</div>
          <h3>UK initiative — overview</h3>
          <p>Five-tier map: legislation → departments → forums → delivery → standards.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href="/governance/legislation">
          <div class="pill pill--info">Policy</div>
          <h3>Legislation &amp; policy</h3>
          <p>DMCC Act 2024, DUA Act 2025, Leasehold &amp; Freehold Reform Act, Industrial Strategy.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href="/governance/departments">
          <div class="pill pill--info">Policy</div>
          <h3>Departments &amp; bodies</h3>
          <p>MHCLG, DSIT, DBT, HMLR, NTSELAT, FCA, ICO — who does what.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href="/governance/steering-forums">
          <div class="pill pill--info">Policy</div>
          <h3>Steering &amp; coordination</h3>
          <p>DPMSG (13 founding members), Smart Data Council, HBSG.</p>
        </a>
      </div>

      <h2 id="opda-organisation">OPDA the organisation</h2>
      <p>Who OPDA is, and the operational vehicle it delivers through.</p>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <a class="card" href="/governance/opda-members">
          <div class="pill pill--info">Members</div>
          <h3>OPDA member firms</h3>
          <p>13 founding members + association members, mapped to bounded contexts. One simple membership tier.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href="/governance/sandbox">
          <div class="pill pill--success">Delivery</div>
          <h3>Trust Framework Sandbox</h3>
          <p>CLC + OPDA + Raidiam, RPF-funded. Operational today.</p>
        </a>
      </div>

      <h2 id="standards-landscape">Standards landscape</h2>
      <p>How PDTF anchors itself to external trust and data-governance frameworks.</p>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <a class="card" href="/governance/toip-governance">
          <div class="pill pill--accent">Alignment</div>
          <h3>ToIP governance model</h3>
          <p>The 4 layers, mapped to OPDA's artefacts. Why ToIP fits a federated trust framework.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href="/governance/strategic-alignment">
          <div class="pill pill--accent">Alignment</div>
          <h3>Strategic alignment</h3>
          <p>HMLR Strategy 2022+, DSIT National Data Strategy, DVSTF, W3C VC, ToIP — how PDTF aligns.</p>
        </a>
      </div>

      <h2 id="opda-rules">OPDA's rules</h2>
      <p>
        Constitutional rules, current procedures and clearly labelled proposals. A page
        describing a proposal does not itself make that proposal authoritative.
      </p>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <a class="card" href="/governance/standards-lifecycle">
          <div class="pill pill--warn">Proposed · ADR-0068</div>
          <h3>Standards lifecycle &amp; ratification</h3>
          <p>How evidence earns human consensus, passes public and independent review, and becomes a ratified OPDA Standard.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href="/governance/change-management">
          <div class="pill pill--info">Rules</div>
          <h3>Change management</h3>
          <p>Constitutional change through the General Assembly and the current 8-step schema implementation procedure.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href="/governance/lifecycle-versioning">
          <div class="pill pill--info">Draft policy</div>
          <h3>Release versioning &amp; retirement</h3>
          <p>Current version domains and the remaining rules for compatibility, deprecation, support and retirement.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href="/governance/conformance-scheme">
          <div class="pill pill--info">Rules</div>
          <h3>Conformance &amp; certification</h3>
          <p>Self-certification today (3-person panel, 80% pass mark). Planned technical conformance follows the Open Banking pattern.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href="/governance/accreditation-directory">
          <div class="pill pill--brand">Rules · new</div>
          <h3>Accreditation Directory</h3>
          <p>Two-axis maturity view per member firm — AL coverage + capability scores. Full spec in ADR 0004.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href="/governance/risk-liability">
          <div class="pill pill--info">Rules</div>
          <h3>Risk &amp; liability</h3>
          <p>Articles cap member liability at £1; framework spec is MIT/AS-IS. Downstream liability still open.</p>
        </a>
      </div>

      <h2 id="operating-model">Operating Model</h2>
      <p>How the framework runs day-to-day: who's accountable, when meetings happen, who engages with stakeholders, how unstructured attachments flow. Adopts DCAM v3's "Operating Model" component name directly.</p>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <a class="card" href="/governance/data-stewardship">
          <div class="pill pill--warn">Operating · proposed</div>
          <h3>Data stewardship &amp; decision rights</h3>
          <p>Domain Working Groups own local meaning; Interoperability owns common boundaries and mappings; independent functions verify; authorised OPDA governance ratifies.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href="/governance/meetings-and-feedback">
          <div class="pill pill--info">Operating</div>
          <h3>Meeting cadence &amp; feedback</h3>
          <p>Meeting cadence, feedback channels, issue disposition, public review and the 10-year constitutional decision-record baseline.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href="/governance/stakeholder-engagement">
          <div class="pill pill--info">Operating</div>
          <h3>Stakeholder engagement</h3>
          <p>Broad standards participation for members, invited non-members, regulators, government and the public—without confusing contribution with corporate authority.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href="/governance/overlay-attachments">
          <div class="pill pill--brand">Operating · new</div>
          <h3>Overlay attachments</h3>
          <p>Per-attachment policy across v3 overlays (TA10 plans, EPCs, leasehold packs, photographs). File formats, signing, retention, consent.</p>
        </a>
      </div>

      <h2 id="quality-security">Quality &amp; security</h2>
      <p>Cross-cutting frameworks every member firm reports against. Fills the two largest gaps in OPDA's published rules (per ADR 0001).</p>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <a class="card" href="/governance/data-quality">
          <div class="pill pill--brand">Quality · new</div>
          <h3>Data quality framework</h3>
          <p>Six dimensions — accuracy, completeness, consistency, timeliness, uniqueness, validity. Per-claim measurement; quarterly reporting via the Accreditation Directory.</p>
        </a>
        <a class="card" href="/governance/data-security">
          <div class="pill pill--brand">Security · new</div>
          <h3>Data security framework</h3>
          <p>KYC/KYB, DID key management, signature verification, revocation, audit logging. Policy + checklist + audit profile per control.</p>
        </a>
      </div>

      <h2 id="status">Status at a glance</h2>

      <p>
        Status here describes the maturity of the website page or proposal—not the maturity
        of an ontology, schema or standards release.
      </p>

      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Artefact</th><th>Status</th><th>Where</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>UK initiative overview</td><td>✅ Built</td><td><a href="/governance/uk-initiative">/governance/uk-initiative</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Legislation &amp; policy backbone</td><td>✅ Built</td><td><a href="/governance/legislation">/governance/legislation</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Departments &amp; bodies</td><td>✅ Built</td><td><a href="/governance/departments">/governance/departments</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Steering &amp; coordination forums</td><td>✅ Built</td><td><a href="/governance/steering-forums">/governance/steering-forums</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>OPDA member firms</td><td>✅ Built</td><td><a href="/governance/opda-members">/governance/opda-members</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Trust Framework Sandbox</td><td>✅ Built</td><td><a href="/governance/sandbox">/governance/sandbox</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>ToIP governance model</td><td>✅ Built</td><td><a href="/governance/toip-governance">/governance/toip-governance</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Strategic alignment</td><td>✅ Built</td><td><a href="/governance/strategic-alignment">/governance/strategic-alignment</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Conformance &amp; certification</td><td>✅ Draft</td><td><a href="/governance/conformance-scheme">/governance/conformance-scheme</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Accreditation Directory</td><td>📋 Spec (ADR 0004) · ✅ Draft page</td><td><a href="/governance/accreditation-directory">/governance/accreditation-directory</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Change management</td><td>✅ Draft</td><td><a href="/governance/change-management">/governance/change-management</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Standards lifecycle &amp; ratification</td><td>⚠️ Proposed — not yet operative</td><td><a href="/governance/standards-lifecycle">/governance/standards-lifecycle</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Release versioning &amp; retirement</td><td>✅ Draft page · policy incomplete</td><td><a href="/governance/lifecycle-versioning">/governance/lifecycle-versioning</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Risk &amp; liability</td><td>✅ Draft</td><td><a href="/governance/risk-liability">/governance/risk-liability</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Data stewardship &amp; decision rights</td><td>⚠️ Proposed operating model</td><td><a href="/governance/data-stewardship">/governance/data-stewardship</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Meetings, feedback &amp; decision records</td><td>⚠️ Mixed status · proposal clearly labelled</td><td><a href="/governance/meetings-and-feedback">/governance/meetings-and-feedback</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Stakeholder engagement</td><td>⚠️ Mixed status · proposal clearly labelled</td><td><a href="/governance/stakeholder-engagement">/governance/stakeholder-engagement</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Overlay attachments policy</td><td>🚧 Stub · Technical WG</td><td><a href="/governance/overlay-attachments">/governance/overlay-attachments</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Data quality framework</td><td>✅ Draft · C&amp;R WG</td><td><a href="/governance/data-quality">/governance/data-quality</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Data security framework</td><td>✅ Draft · C&amp;R WG</td><td><a href="/governance/data-security">/governance/data-security</a></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
</Layout>
